<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:34:57 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe</link><description>
The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months, and countries must claim and account for the remaining funds.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">efd12616-c634-11f1-8f6e-b3d04d2883e3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:19:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png">© FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon</link><description>
The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c522638-c642-11f1-ab3a-5f09709176c3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:05:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile</link><description>
NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46b25518-c63a-11f1-a40f-2dd75a13a6e7</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:41:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg">© Nicolas Maetermink, Belga / AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage</link><description>
And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f93dadda-c636-11f1-abe7-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-131234-133046-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f93dadda-c636-11f1-abe7-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-131234-133046-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe8bc60a-c636-11f1-b4ca-75ff764c78f1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:26:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media</link><description>
An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc19ab6-c630-11f1-b68c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-120216-120402-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc19ab6-c630-11f1-b68c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-120216-120402-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12fd2522-c630-11f1-a33c-2bb1d710b13a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:24:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Prison 'Games of Hope' olympics in Italy unite inmates and staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff</link><description>
Sport has the power to unite, and overcome barriers... In Rome, inmates and prison officers became athletes for the day, and took part in a sort of mini prison olympics. Organised by the John Paul II foundation for sport, this is the third edition of the “Games of Hope”, over a year after it was held in the men's wing of the prison in 2025. Story by Emily Boyle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe1e4916-c629-11f1-b215-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-091213-091346-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe1e4916-c629-11f1-b215-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-091213-091346-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0308d720-c62a-11f1-9855-31f546c55914</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:54:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland: Police foils alleged assassination attempt against PM</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm</link><description>
Poland's interior ministry said Sunday a man had been detained on suspicion of plotting an attack against Prime Minister Donald Tusk and Defence minister Wladyslaw Kosiniak-Kamysz. Interior minister Marcin Kierwinski told Polish media that the suspect, a man in his 60s, had been arrested in the southwestern region of Lower Silesia. He was identified through an analysis of content posted online. The man's home is being searched and his contacts examined. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Warsaw, Adrien Sarlat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e7d13e6-c62a-11f1-9df1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100343-100644-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e7d13e6-c62a-11f1-9df1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100343-100644-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">636f9d9c-c62a-11f1-a4cf-1b9a714fd227</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:52:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Are European automakers capable of withstanding Chinese competition?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition</link><description>
The Paris Motor Show opens its doors today, and with it come mounting economic and diplomatic issues. The European Union has just announced that it has secured a commitment from China to moderate the flow of hybrid vehicles into the block's market. It opens the prospect of cutting China's export by more than a half and could prevent millions of Chinese cars from being shipped to Europe. Are European automakers capable of withstanding this competition and their dependence on China? This report from France 2 and Morgan Ayre.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b23c0e66-c624-11f1-b7ee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-084242-084440-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b23c0e66-c624-11f1-b7ee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-084242-084440-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b748f7f2-c624-11f1-b11a-019eccf14e4d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:26:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky says surprised to hear about Trump's 'energy ceasefire' between Ukraine and Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia</link><description>
Ukrainian power plants were hit by Russian strikes on Sunday, leading to power outages. President Volodymyr Zelensky announced the attacks and expressed his surprise at the US President's post that stated that an “energy ceasefire” had been agreed upon between Ukraine and Russia. While Zelensky said he was not aware of any deal he said he would welcome one. Moscow has yet to confirm any accord. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1f72c30-c55b-11f1-941b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T204400Z-1727445418-RC2WZNAE754C-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-USA-DIESEL-UKRAINE-ZELENSKIY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1f72c30-c55b-11f1-941b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T204400Z-1727445418-RC2WZNAE754C-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-USA-DIESEL-UKRAINE-ZELENSKIY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">704c058e-c623-11f1-ac63-8b5dc0aa6046</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:19:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Americans Robert E. Hall and Michael Woodford win Nobel Prize in Economics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics</link><description>
The 2026 Nobel economics prize has been awarded to US economists ⁠Robert Hall ​and Michael Woodford, the Royal Swedish Academy of ‌Sciences said on Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bbb0170-c61d-11f1-b601-83431ceca236</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:54:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg">© Nobel Prize Outreach</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump touts surprise 'energy ceasefire' – Zelensky says he hasn't seen details, Moscow silent</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-%E2%80%93-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent</link><description>
The US President Donald Trump sowed confusion on Sunday, announcing an "energy ceasefire" between Ukraine and Russia. Kyiv expressed astonishment, there was silence from Moscow. Ukrainian strikes have wreaked havoc on the Russian oil industry. Were there to be an "energy ceasefire" it could allow Moscow to repair refineries. For Ukraine, it could safeguard vital energy infrastructure. Story by Nicholas Rushworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db49974e-c61d-11f1-b573-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T004527Z-1640129275-RC2O0OA8PKYS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db49974e-c61d-11f1-b573-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T004527Z-1640129275-RC2O0OA8PKYS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3baeba8e-c61d-11f1-9666-2f42f8430027</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:19:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia targets Ukraine energy facilities despite Trump ceasefire announcement</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-live-oil-prices-fall-after-trump-unilaterally-announces-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire</link><description>
Russia continued to attack multiple power plants in Ukraine on Monday, in spite of claims by US President Donald yesterday stating a so-called “energy ceasefire” had been agreed to. NATO chief said that the military alliance would “block, blunt and break” any Russian attack on its members’ territory. Meanwhile strikes on civilians continue, with a 13-year-old girl  among three killed in the country's east. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d12228a-c65f-11f1-a46a-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2XZ6NE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d12228a-c65f-11f1-a46a-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2XZ6NE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3bfb300-c5f7-11f1-9614-034b6590089e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:29:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d12228a-c65f-11f1-a46a-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2XZ6NE.jpg">© Sergey Bobok, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO top commander to warn Russia over alliance’s ability to counter-attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-top-commander-warn-russia-alliance-counter-attack</link><description>
NATO’s top military commander is expected to warn Russia on Monday that the alliance can counter any attack, officials said. US General Alexus Grynkewich will outline his “theory of victory” at a Warsaw security conference amid Western concerns over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Ukraine’s wartime backers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">581055e2-c5dd-11f1-9d70-9d438446f071</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:41:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg">© Nicolas Maeterlinck, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Slovenia rejects bill in blow to PM Janez Jansa’s reform agenda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-slovenia-bill-pm-janez-jansa-reform</link><description>
Slovenians rejected a bill expanding parliamentary inquiry powers in a referendum Sunday, dealing a blow to nationalist Prime Minister Janez Jansa. With 99 percent of votes counted, 51 percent opposed the proposal and 49 percent backed it in the binding vote. The opposition had denounced his reform agenda as "authoritarian".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98813ac8-ac0c-11f1-a9b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/f7359e93a9fdc8275228248f1acc565e3d957d05.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98813ac8-ac0c-11f1-a9b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/f7359e93a9fdc8275228248f1acc565e3d957d05.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d2d94ac4-c5bd-11f1-b563-51a17e536ff6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:01:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98813ac8-ac0c-11f1-a9b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/f7359e93a9fdc8275228248f1acc565e3d957d05.jpg">© Jure Makovec, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK PM Burnham warns French voters of Russian political influence on back of Brexit vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-uk-pm-burnham-warns-french-voters-of-russian-political-influence-on-back-of-brexit-vote</link><description>
British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Sunday warned French and German voters of potential for Russian influence in upcoming elections, on the back of "clear" interference in Britain's referendum on European Union membership in 2016. Russia has previously denied meddling in the Brexit vote, while former British leader Boris Johnson 2020 also said there was no evidence of interference. Burnham made the comments in an interview with The Rest is Politics podcast, released on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a04c029e-c5aa-11f1-afc4-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QZ4AD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a04c029e-c5aa-11f1-afc4-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QZ4AD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b08c1848-c5a9-11f1-b3ac-ddae93034708</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:42:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a04c029e-c5aa-11f1-afc4-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QZ4AD.jpg">© AFP, Christopher Furlon</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Ukraine: Coerced into a corner?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261011-ukraine-coerced-into-a-corner</link><description>
It's reported that Ukraine is right now facing intense diplomatic pressure and coercion from the Trump administration to end the war quickly.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4768d690-c599-11f1-bdd5-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-YouTube-interview-simple-jaune-rouge-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4768d690-c599-11f1-bdd5-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-YouTube-interview-simple-jaune-rouge-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0fee0db4-c596-11f1-b6b4-e746747508da</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:36:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>New Russian strikes follow Trump's announcement of Russia-Ukraine energy ceasefire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire</link><description>
US President Trump said Sunday via social media platform Truth Social that Russia and Ukraine had agreed to an energy ceasefire. Neither Kyiv nor Moscow confirmed the agreement, but Zelensky later confirmed new Russian strikes to a Ukrainian powerplant. Additional reports suggest at least 5 have been killed and other civilians injured in strikes in the cities of Kharkiv and Ivano-Frankivsk.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0873ab7c-c580-11f1-b3d3-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284044155459.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0873ab7c-c580-11f1-b3d3-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284044155459.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a4cc5de-c580-11f1-b389-2392262d07b9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:39:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0873ab7c-c580-11f1-b3d3-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26284044155459.jpg">© Nathan Howard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: French student protests, October 7 anniversary and Adenot's return to Earth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-earth</link><description>
Blockades and protests by French secondary school and university students continued, occasionally becoming violent; French astronaut Sophie Adenot returned to Earth after eight months aboard the International Space Station; Israel's commemorations marking the three-year anniversary of the October 7 attacks: here's a look back at some of the most striking images from the past week's news.
